+Paper grounding (Step 0).  Section 2 defines an isogeny as a nonconstant
+algebraic group map with finite kernel.  Proposition "Horizontal and vertical
+isogenies" and the isogeny-graph definition in Section 6 identify graph edges
+with prime-degree isogenies.  Section 7's theorem "Supersingular graphs are
