One canonicalization gap surfaced in the final audit: translating the starting x-coordinate by one of its 2-torsion roots preserves the first quotient and therefore the whole problem, but the G8 test only exercised scalings and Frobenius. I’m adding that real curve-model relabeling and its composition with the existing symmetries, then I’ll regenerate the report.
