Implemented a native Track A supersingular 2-isogeny path generator based on the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.04062).

Deliverables:

- [gen_1711_04062.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1711.04062/gen_1711_04062.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1711.04062/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1711.04062/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1711.04062/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1711.04062/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1711.04062/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000.
- All four adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes.
- Standard meet-in-the-middle baseline: 524,512 nodes, 16.74 seconds.
- Complete frontier estimate: 1,342,177,280 leaves.
- Answer: 1,564 characters, 58 atoms.
- Canonical-key tests: 60/60 invariant and carried-witness checks.

The only blocker is external: all 12 oracle calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” They are correctly recorded as errors, not model failures, so no LLM-hardening verdict is claimed. Once quota is restored, rerun `harden.py`, rerun both G9 scratch arms, update `G9_ORACLE_RESULTS`, and regenerate the self-test report.
