Rejected and archived rather than shipped.

The full paper defines isogeny-graph vertices as \(j\)-invariants, while the existing checker required equality of coordinate-normalized curve models. A target-only coordinate change reproduced the defect: identical \(j\)-invariant and canonical key, but `verify` rejected the witness.

Repairing that mismatch still fails G9(c). For \(e=58\), the paper’s meet-in-the-middle method requires a \(2^{29}=536{,}870{,}912\)-entry frontier—far above the 300-operation cap, with no shorter Track B route described in the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1711.04062v1).

